A||||2||Gokart||Body shop question||||5||
Z||000000||Gokart||06-01-2000||04:05 AM||||I hope you painting/buffing experts can tell me WHAT HAPPENED! I painted my trunk scoop and the color was a perfect match, but it had slight orange peel so I wet sanded it(600to1200)then buffed the shine back with a micro-finish liquid. Now it's a lighter red than before, almost the bright red on most Fieros and mines medium red, but when I get it wet with water it's a perfect match again! Did I not buff it enough? Is there a different product I should be buffing it with? Thanks for any suggestions! ||||reg||5
Z||000001||rogergarrison||06-01-2000||12:53 PM||||ive owned my own body shop for 30 yrs. First u didnt say if you painted with single stage or basecoat/clearcoat. If it clearcoat and you didnt sand thru to basecoat, it couldnt have 'changed' the color. Could it be the surrounding part of the car need some rubbing out too? If you paint a hood and not the fenders, even if they look fine, you may have to rub out the fenders too to get a match. If you painted single stage color, the only way it could have changed is if you painted another shade of red under it first and sanded thru, or sanded enough off that primer coat is showing thru,assuming you used gray primer. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Gokart||06-02-2000||07:03 AM||||Thanks Roger! That was it! I forgot NAPA mixed the wrong color the first time and after I painted it I discovered it was the bright red that most red Fieros are. I had them remix to the right color and forgot all this when I sanded the orange peel! Yah, I sanded it right down to the other red! That worked out ok though cause I re-painted it last night and this time it came out sweet! No sanding/buffing required <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||14
